# Implementation Plan: Exposing Runtime Metrics to Client

## Overview
This plan exposes runtime metrics (queue depth, turn counts, invalid outputs, action stats) to the client via a new `runtime.metrics` message type without breaking existing protocol guarantees.

## 1. Type/Interface Changes

### File: `packages/protocol/src/messages.ts`

**Add new metric types:**
```typescript
export type RuntimeMetrics = {
  queueDepth: number;
  turnsCompleted: number;
  turnsFailed: number;
  turnsInterrupted: number;
  invalidOutputs: number;
  actionsApplied: number;
  actionsRejected: number;
  uptimeMs: number;
};
```

**Extend `ServerMessage` union:**
```typescript
| {
    version: Version;
    type: "runtime.metrics";
    payload: RuntimeMetrics;
  }
```

**Add Zod schema for metrics:**
```typescript
const runtimeMetricsSchema = z.object({
  queueDepth: z.number().int().nonnegative(),
  turnsCompleted: z.number().int().nonnegative(),
  turnsFailed: z.number().int().nonnegative(),
  turnsInterrupted: z.number().int().nonnegative(),
  invalidOutputs: z.number().int().nonnegative(),
  actionsApplied: z.number().int().nonnegative(),
  actionsRejected: z.number().int().nonnegative(),
  uptimeMs: z.number().int().nonnegative()
});
```

## 2. Runtime Wiring

### File: `apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/GameRuntimeServer.ts`

**Add metrics tracking state:**
```typescript
private readonly metricsStart = Date.now();
```

**Update `MetricsTracker` interface (if needed):**
Check `MetricsTracker` implementation to ensure it exposes:
- `queueDepth`
- `turnsCompleted`
- `turnsFailed`
- `turnsInterrupted`
- `invalidOutputs`
- `actionsApplied`
- `actionsRejected`

If `MetricsTracker` doesn't expose these, add methods:
```typescript
// In metrics.ts (if it exists)
export class MetricsTracker {
  // ... existing methods ...

  snapshot(): RuntimeMetrics {
    return {
      queueDepth: this.queueDepth,
      turnsCompleted: this.turnsCompleted,
      turnsFailed: this.turnsFailed,
      turnsInterrupted: this.turnsInterrupted,
      invalidOutputs: this.invalidOutputs,
      actionsApplied: this.actionsApplied,
      actionsRejected: this.actionsRejected,
      uptimeMs: Date.now() - this.metricsStart
    };
  }
}
```

**Add metrics emission in `tick()` method:**
```typescript
private tick(): void {
  // ... existing logic ...

  this.metrics.setQueueDepth(this.totalQueuedActions());
  this.sendWorldSnapshot();

  // Emit metrics snapshot
  this.emitMessage({
    version: PROTOCOL_VERSION,
    type: "runtime.metrics",
    payload: this.metrics.snapshot()
  });
}
```

**Add metrics emission in `persistSession()` method:**
```typescript
private async persistSession(): Promise<void> {
  // ... existing logic ...

  const sessionSnapshot: SessionSnapshot = {
    seed: this.seed,
    tick: snapshot.tick,
    threadIds: this.threadIds,
    metrics: this.metrics.snapshot(), // Already exists
    simulation: simulationState
  };
  await this.stateStore.save(sessionSnapshot);
}
```

## 3. Client Wiring

### File: `apps/game-client/src/App.tsx`

**Add metrics state:**
```typescript
const [metrics, setMetrics] = useState<RuntimeMetrics | null>(null);
```

**Add metrics handler in WebSocket message switch:**
```typescript
case "runtime.metrics":
  setMetrics(message.payload);
  return;
```

**Add metrics display in HUD:**
```typescript
<div className="hud-card">
  <button
    type="button"
    className="hud-card-toggle"
    onClick={() => toggleHudSection("metrics")}
    aria-expanded={!collapsedHudSections.metrics}
  >
    <span>Runtime Metrics</span>
    <span className="hud-card-toggle-icon">{collapsedHudSections.metrics ? "+" : "-"}</span>
  </button>
  {!collapsedHudSections.metrics ? (
    metrics ? (
      <div className="hud-grid">
        <p>Queue Depth</p>
        <p>{metrics.queueDepth}</p>
        <p>Turns Completed</p>
        <p>{metrics.turnsCompleted}</p>
        <p>Turns Failed</p>
        <p>{metrics.turnsFailed}</p>
        <p>Invalid Outputs</p>
        <p>{metrics.invalidOutputs}</p>
        <p>Actions Applied</p>
        <p>{metrics.actionsApplied}</p>
        <p>Actions Rejected</p>
        <p>{metrics.actionsRejected}</p>
        <p>Uptime</p>
        <p>{Math.floor(metrics.uptimeMs / 60000)}m {Math.floor((metrics.uptimeMs % 60000) / 1000)}s</p>
      </div>
    ) : (
      <p className="muted">No metrics</p>
    )
  ) : null}
</div>
```

**Update `HudSectionKey` type:**
```typescript
type HudSectionKey = 
  | "selectedAgent" 
  | "score" 
  | "social" 
  | "agents" 
  | "inventory" 
  | "crafting" 
  | "buildables"
  | "metrics";
```

**Update initial collapsed state:**
```typescript
const [collapsedHudSections, setCollapsedHudSections] = useState<Record<HudSectionKey, boolean>>({
  selectedAgent: false,
  score: false,
  social: false,
  agents: false,
  inventory: false,
  crafting: false,
  buildables: false,
  metrics: false
});
```

